hermes-nabu includes code from the Hermes Gadget SDK
https://github.com/Adolanium/hermes-gadget-sdk (commit 66b4af0f)

Copied from firmware/drivers/ unchanged:
  main/shared_reply.hpp
  main/speaker_queue.hpp
  main/wifi_retry.hpp
  main/ws_link.hpp

Copied from firmware/esp32/main/ unchanged:
  main/port_buttons.cpp
  main/port_events.cpp
  main/port_storage.cpp
  main/port_system.cpp
  main/port_ws.cpp

Copied from firmware/esp32/main/ and modified:
  main/port.hpp           trimmed to the drivers this board uses, plus
                          ButtonConfig from board.hpp
  main/port_console.cpp   without the wifi-setup command
  main/port_wifi.cpp      station mode only, no phone setup network,
                          Wi-Fi power save off
  main/Kconfig.projbuild  defaults menu only

The core (firmware/core) is not copied; the ESP-IDF component manager
fetches it at the commit pinned in main/idf_component.yml.

The board drivers are written for this project. The hardware facts they rely
on come from ESPHome ("esphome", https://github.com/esphome/esphome) and the
stock Voice PE firmware ("voice-pe",
https://github.com/esphome/home-assistant-voice-pe):
  pin mapping                    voice-pe: home-assistant-voice.yaml
  dial steps and volume arc      voice-pe: home-assistant-voice.yaml
  LED colors and animations      voice-pe: home-assistant-voice.yaml
  AIC3204 DAC init sequence      esphome: esphome/components/aic3204
  XMOS pipeline-stage protocol   voice-pe: esphome/components/voice_kit
No code from either project is copied.

